      "title": "Developer fixture: learn two directions",
      "summary": "Unbundled workspace acceptance fixture only.",
      "objective": "Keep the supplied uplink settings. Teach the office and archive switches where the opposite workstation sends from, so a frame from a to 02:00:00:00:00:03 follows known-unicast forwarding and reaches only c. Use sends to build the learned state; Check work tests the current table and forwarding.",
      "difficulty": "Beginner",
      "minutes": 15,
      "steps": [
        "Inspect the supplied addresses and connections.",
        "Send from the archive, then from the office.",
        "Check work and inspect the current result."
      ],
      "guide": [],
      "explanation": "This private fixture establishes no curriculum coverage. The two directions can be learned in either order; probes clone the current state independently.",
      "hints": [
        "The archive workstation must send before the office switch knows its source."
      ],
      "sources": [
        "https://www.cisco.com/c/en/us/td/docs/switches/lan/c9000/lyr2-fwd/cdp-lldp-mac-udld/cdp-lldp-mac-udld-configuration-guide/c-configure-mac.html"
      ],
      "simplifications": "Developer fixture, sources checked2026-10-24. Individual Ethernet metadata only; finite virtual topology, manual time, no IOS terminal, IP, ARP, hardware timing, STP or real frames. Seeded old entries are a separate disclosed diagnostic boundary.",
